{"qid":"Q213","names":["Czech Republic"],"title":"Czech Republic","endonym":{"native":"Česko","lang":"cs"},"capsule":"The Czech Republic (Česko / Czechia) came into existence on 1 January 1993 when Czechoslovakia dissolved peacefully into two successor states, with Václav Havel becoming the first president and inheriting the Bohemian lands, Moravia, and Czech Silesia. It joined NATO in 1999 and the European Union in 2004, cementing its post-communist Western orientation; by the 2010s it had one of the highest per-capita incomes in Central and Eastern Europe. In 2016 the government formally promoted the short-form name Česko / Czechia for international use. As of 2025 the republic is a parliamentary democracy with Petr Pavel as president following elections held in January 2023.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Modern state boundaries are precisely mapped and internationally recognised; the Wikidata attestation window 1992–2025 reflects post-dissolution continuity and is unambiguous.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Czech Republic","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Czech_Republic"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Dissolution of Czechoslovakia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dissolution_of_Czechoslovakia"}],"britannica":"place/Czech-Republic","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Czech Republic","rulers":[{"qid":"Q36233","name":"Václav Havel","start":1993,"end":2003,"image":"Václav Havel cut out.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/V%C3%A1clav%20Havel%20cut%20out.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","artist":"Ondřej Sláma","attributionRequired":true}},{